    fix(routing): attribute the routing-swap notice to the matched rule; honor --quiet

    Addresses the 2026-07-23 maphew/mybd review on gastownhall/beads#4866
    (fix/contributor-role-visibility). printContributorRoutingNotice was
    hardcoded to blame beads.role=contributor and recommend
    `git config beads.role maintainer` for every routed read, even when the
    swap was actually caused by routing.maintainer or the unconditional
    routing.default fallback (internal/routing.DetermineTargetRepo) -
    misdiagnosing the cause in those cases.

    - internal/routing: DetermineTargetRepo now delegates to a new
      DetermineTargetRepoWithRule, which also reports which rule matched
      (RuleContributor/RuleMaintainer/RuleDefault/RuleExplicitOverride/RuleNone).
    - cmd/bd/routing_read.go: thread that rule out of
      determineAutoRoutedRepoPath and openRoutedReadStore, and branch
      printContributorRoutingNotice's text and remediation command on it via
      routingNoticeText, so a maintainer- or default-routed swap gets its own
      accurate wording instead of the contributor-role message.
    - Gate the notice on !quietFlag, matching quietFlag's documented contract
      ("Suppress non-essential output (errors only)") and the other
      non-error stderr notices in this package (tips.go, metrics.go).
    - Reword the parenthetical issue count to "this project has N total
      issue(s)" rather than claiming all N are "hidden as a result" of
      routing, since stats.TotalIssues is an unfiltered COUNT(*) that
      includes closed/deferred/blocked issues bd ready would never surface
      anyway; comment the GetStatistics-error fallback (count omitted)
      as an explicit decision.
    - Add routing_notice_test.go covering each rule variant's notice text
      and --quiet suppression; update the existing openRoutedReadStore/
      determineAutoRoutedRepoPath tests for the new return signatures.

